# LaTeX file and folder names

Book folders keep the pattern `Tyranids 300` and `Rulebook 303`. New French codices are **v3.1.0** → folder digits **310** (`Tyranids 310`). Those 3.1.0 PDFs in `Originals/` are early drafts; the French authors are still writing them. French PDFs stay in `Originals/` with their original names.

Each book has `main.tex` as the root and `preamble.tex` for local setup.

Shared preambles nest. `shared/preamble-master.tex` has the common setup (A4, tables, `\unitdivider`, section page breaks). Codices `\input{../shared/codex-preamble}` and the rulebook `\input{../shared/rulebook-preamble}`; those files `\input{../shared/preamble-master}`. Codex extras (subsection minipages, `\unitimage`) stay in `codex-preamble`. Book-specific extras stay in the local `preamble.tex`.

- Codex: flat folder, one kebab-case file per section (`special-rules.tex`)
- Rulebook: numbered kebab-case chapter folders (`01-game-turn/movement-phase.tex`)
- Images: `figures/`, kebab-case (`movement-a.png`)

Names use only lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens. No spaces, underscores, or accents.

`\input{legal-notice}` — do not include the `.tex` suffix.
